after "\"id\":1," "M!{\"id\":2,\"msg\":{\"filesystem\":{\"write\":{\"path\":\"/projects/Five w"
then +20ms "ire/README.md\",\"data\":\"# five-wire\\n\\nFive wires over four RMT s"
then +20ms "lots, on the DOM-Z-102's own pins \xe2\x80\x94 the project the\\n**second "
then +20ms "wave** needs in order to exist at all.\\n\\n`lp-fw/fw-esp32v3`'s b"
then +20ms "lock plan caps the pool at `POOLED_SLOT_CAP = 4`\\ntwo-block slot"
then +20ms "s (`v3_rmt.rs`), so a fifth wire cannot have a slot of its own:\\"
then +20ms "nit time-shares one by per-transmission pad muxing, a `func_out_"
then +20ms "sel_cfg` write\\nbetween waves (`wire_pusher.rs`). That second wa"
then +20ms "ve only runs on the product\\npath, driven by mailbox posts from "
then +20ms "the PRO core, so the only way to exercise\\nit is a project that "
then +20ms "really declares five outputs. This is that project.\\n\\n| Port | "
then +20ms "Endpoint | Lamps | Channels |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 0 | `ws281x:"
then +20ms "local:IO18` | 16 | 0..16 |\\n| 1 | `ws281x:local:IO16` | 16 | 16."
then +20ms ".32 |\\n| 2 | `ws281x:local:IO14` | 16 | 32..48 |\\n| 3 | `ws281x:"
then +20ms "local:IO2` | 16 | 48..64 |\\n| 4 | `ws281x:local:IO13` | the rest"
then +20ms " (16) | 64..80 |\\n\\nThe four fused DATA terminals plus `IO13`, t"
then +20ms "he claimable spare \xe2\x80\x94 the board's\\nown five-wire shape (`lp-cor"
then +20ms "e/lpc-hardware/boards/domraem/dom-z-102.json`, and\\nits `measure"
then +20ms "d` note: *5 wires \xc3\x97 300 LEDs at 29.99 fps, 240 s soak on the\\nd"
then +20ms "ual-core pusher build*). Only the highest-keyed port may omit it"
then +20ms "s `count`; it\\nmeans \\\"the rest of the buffer\\\".\\n\\n## The three"
then +20ms " constraints, and what breaks if you relax one\\n\\n**No clock, an"
then +20ms "d no `time` input.** `shader.glsl` is\\n`projects/test/shader-ora"
then +20ms "cle/shader.glsl`, byte for byte, and for the same\\nreason: every"
then +20ms " frame is identical, so *\\\"every wire's frames are the same\\nfra"
then +20ms "me\\\"* is a statement about the machine rather than about when it"
then +20ms " was\\nsampled. Add a clock and a per-frame checksum comparison s"
then +20ms "tops meaning\\nanything.\\n\\n**Five distinct wires.** The five pat"
then +20ms "hs sample five different rows of the\\nrender, so the five wires "
then +20ms "carry five different byte strings. A routing\\nmix-up \xe2\x80\x94 two pad"
then +20ms "s driven from one channel, a slot handed to the wrong wire \xe2\x80\x94\\n"
then +20ms "then shows up as two wires with the same checksum, which is exac"
then +20ms "tly the\\nfailure the second wave can cause. Give every row the s"
then +20ms "ame colour and that\\nevidence disappears.\\n\\n**A neutral output "
then +20ms "pipeline.** `white_point [1,1,1]`, brightness 1, LUT,\\ndithering"
then +20ms " and interpolation all off, gamma off \xe2\x80\x94 the same neutral setti"
then +20ms "ng the\\noracle project documents. Under exactly that configurati"
then +20ms "on `DisplayPipeline`\\nis stateless, so the bytes on the wire are"
then +20ms " the engine's samples and a frame\\nis a function of the project "
then +20ms "alone.\\n\\n## Where it is used\\n\\n- `lp-emu/esp/lp-emu-esp32v3/te"
then +20ms "sts/five_wires.rs` \xe2\x80\x94 the emulator's five-wire\\n  gate: five pa"
then +20ms "ds routed, a re-mux visible between waves, and each wire's\\n  de"
then +20ms "coded frames checksum-equal to that endpoint's own\\n  `[OUT] fra"
then +20ms "me=\xe2\x80\xa6 crc=` summary line.\\n- `lp-emu/esp/lp-emu-esp32v3/walks/f"
then +20ms "ive-wire.script` \xe2\x80\x94 the `lp-cli upload` of\\n  this project, cap"
then +20ms "tured live and replayed in guest time.\\n\\nIt is not a demo. Sixt"
then +20ms "een lamps a wire is deliberately small: the whole point\\nis the "
then +20ms "slot arithmetic, and a wire long enough to be pretty costs emula"
then +20ms "ted\\nseconds without changing what is being measured.\\n\"}}}}\n"
